### Operation

- **Accounts/data:** use a dedicated least-privilege synthetic account per concurrent region, secret-managed credentials, and stable dashboard data. Exclude tagged synthetic traffic from customer analytics, billing, notifications, and real-user SLO calculations; retain separate probe availability metrics.
- **Schedule:** propose every five minutes from regions representing your users; for a global service, begin with three regions. Prevent overlapping runs using the same account. Exercise the real authentication mechanism, including an approved MFA/SSO path where applicable.
- **Alerts:** log one failure; warn after two consecutive failures in one region; page on-call after two consecutive failures in two or more regions. Maintain a separate escalation rule for a sustained single-region outage.
- **Evidence:** report `probe=login`, region, severity, last success, duration, failed step, and dashboard/runbook links. Keep diagnostic artifacts access-controlled and free of credentials.
- **Runbook:** name the owner and escalation route; check account/credential health, identity-provider status, recent deploys, and authentication/dashboard telemetry; include manual reproduction steps.

Before enabling production paging, run on staging, deliberately break authentication and dashboard data separately, and verify both failure detection and notification/recovery routing through an agreed test receiver. Review probe health quarterly.

